; Gaussian analogue of beta_notEq_counts_eq_bug.pluck: the evidence combines
; two real_eq observations on the same Gaussian variable with a NOT between
; them, plus a third observation that acts as the "intervening Counts-like"
; accumulation. The conjunction
;     (real_eq x 0.3)  ∧  (real_eq x 0.3)  ∧  ¬(real_eq x 0.3)
; is logically impossible, so P(evidence) = 0 and the posterior must be empty.
;
; Without the GaussianObs.excluded fix, the low-edge of the NOT-wrapped
; real_eq was `spn_one()`, so the chain of merges silently dropped the
; "x ≠ 0.3" constraint and the query phantom-returned True 1.
(query
  (let (x (gaussian 0.0 1.0))
    (Posterior
      True
      (and (real_eq x 0.3)
           (and (real_eq x 0.3)
                (not (real_eq x 0.3)))))))
